---
const rows = [
  ["tall", "taller", "tallest"],
  ["nice", "nicer", "nicest"],
  ["happy", "happier", "happiest"],
  ["big", "bigger", "biggest"],
  ["careful", "more careful", "most careful"],
  ["good", "better", "best"],
  ["bad", "worse", "worst"]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Adjectives - Describing and comparing</h1>
  <p>
    An <strong>adjective</strong> gives information about a noun or pronoun: “a <strong>heavy</strong> bag”;
    “The bag is <strong>heavy</strong>.” Adjectives often come before a noun, but they can also follow a
    linking verb.
  </p>
  <section class="summary-block summary-yellow">
    <h2>Comparing</h2>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Basic</th>
          <th class="th-rule" scope="col">Comparative: two</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Superlative: a group</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          rows.map(([basic, comparative, superlative]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{basic}</th>
              <td>{comparative}</td>
              <td>{superlative}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
  <p>
    Short adjectives usually add <strong>-er</strong> and <strong>-est</strong>. Longer ones usually take
    <strong>more</strong> and <strong>most</strong>. Some have their own forms, such as
    <strong>good → better → best</strong>. <em>Clever</em> allows both <strong>cleverer</strong> and
    <strong>more clever</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    An adjective describes a noun. An adverb can describe an action: “The <strong>quick</strong> runner
    moved <strong>quickly</strong>.” With a linking verb, keep the adjective: “The soup smells
    <strong>wonderful</strong>.”
  </p>
  <p class="try-it">
    <strong>Try it.</strong> Find the adjectives in “The tiny silver key opened the door.” Complete: “Of the
    three roads, this is the (wide) ______.”
  </p>
  <div class="trap-card trap-compact">
    <section class="trap">
      <h2>Don’t double the comparison</h2>
      <p>
        more taller / most tallest
        <span class="mark mark-no" aria-label="Incorrect">✕</span>
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>taller</strong> / <strong>tallest</strong>
        <span class="mark mark-yes" aria-label="Correct">✓</span>
      </p>
      <p>
        gooder / goodest
        <span class="mark mark-no" aria-label="Incorrect">✕</span>
        <strong>better</strong> / <strong>best</strong>
        <span class="mark mark-yes" aria-label="Correct">✓</span>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
